---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/PageLayout.astro";

const root = "/temporal-research-agent";
const video = `${root}/demo/out/temporal-literature-review-demo.mp4`;
const poster = `${root}/deck-assets/worker-killed.png`;
---

<PageLayout
  title="Temporal brings a research pipeline back to life"
  kicker="Temporal case study"
  intro="Improving the durability of our research pipeline using Temporal's Python SDK"
  description="A faithful rewrite of a ten-episode podcast research pipeline as a Python Temporal Workflow, with complete source, recorded failure evidence, and implementation notes."
  image={poster}
  noindex={true}
>
  <article class="tra stack">
    <nav class="tra__artifacts" aria-label="Project artifacts">
      <a href={`${root}/deck.html`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the deck <span>↗</span></a>
      <a href={`${root}/readme`}>Read the README <span>→</span></a>
      <a href="#code-comparison">Compare the code <span>↓</span></a>
      <a href={`${root}/research-output`}>Read the research output <span>→</span></a>
    </nav>

    <figure class="tra__media">
      <video controls preload="metadata" poster={poster}>
        <source src={video} type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
      <figcaption>
        The Worker dies with two research Activities in flight; Temporal Web
        shows both retries and the completed episode and series-review outputs.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="tra__premise prose">
      <h2>The original pipeline already had real business logic</h2>
      <p>
        A JavaScript workflow in the
        <a href="https://www.sjarmak.ai/projects/code-intelligence-digest">Code Intelligence Digest project</a>
        sent ten podcast episodes through
        <a href="https://www.sjarmak.ai/projects/scix-agent">SciX retrieval</a>,
        deep dives, and podcast scripts, then produced two literature reviews.
        The complete source includes every episode brief, seed list, and
        editorial prompt contract. One client process held the active phase
        and in-flight promises.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Python rewrite preserves that dependency graph. A Temporal
        Workflow owns episode order, bounded concurrency, completion policy,
        progress, and final fan-in. Temporal Activities own MCP calls, writer
        calls, heartbeats, clock reads, and artifact I/O.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="code-comparison" class="tra__section">
      <header class="tra__section-head">
        <p class="kicker">The code sample</p>
        <h2>The dependency graph stays recognizable</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="tra__code">
        <section>
          <h3>Before source</h3>
          <pre><code>phase('Research')
await pipeline(
  EPS,
  (it) =&gt; agent(researchPrompt(it)),
  (research, it) =&gt; agent(deepDivePrompt(it, research)),
  (deepDive, it) =&gt; agent(scriptPrompt(it, deepDive)),
)

phase('Synthesis')
await parallel(literatureReviews)</code></pre>
          <p>Condensed here; the code reader contains all 124 source lines.</p>
          <a href={`${root}/code/before`}>Open the complete annotated JavaScript</a>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>After source</h3>
          <pre><code>researched = await workflow.execute_activity(
    "research_episode", request, ...)
deep_dive = await workflow.execute_activity(
    "write_deep_dive", DeepDiveRequest(...), ...)
script = await workflow.execute_activity(
    "write_podcast_script", ScriptRequest(...), ...)</code></pre>
          <p class="cluster">
            <a href={`${root}/code/inputs`}>Business inputs</a>
            <a href={`${root}/code/prompts`}>Prompt contracts</a>
            <a href={`${root}/code/workflow`}>Workflow</a>
            <a href={`${root}/code/activities`}>Activities</a>
            <a href={`${root}/code/worker`}>Worker</a>
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tra__section tra__skill">
      <div class="tra__skill-copy">
        <p class="kicker">Separate follow-on work</p>
        <h2>The general research Workflow also has an agent skill</h2>
        <p>
          <code>run-durable-research</code> submits a Workflow and returns its
          identifiers. The calling agent can exit. Another agent on the same
          workstation can query progress or retrieve the cited report and
          provenance manifest later.
        </p>
        <p>
          This skill wraps the separate general-purpose literature-review
          Workflow. The assignment itself uses the faithful
          <code>PodcastResearchWorkflow</code> shown above. Both keep
          orchestration in a Temporal Workflow and perform
          <a href="https://www.sjarmak.ai/projects/scix-agent">SciX</a>,
          <a href="https://www.sjarmak.ai/projects/code-intelligence-digest">Code Intelligence Digest</a>,
          artifact I/O, and model calls in Temporal Activities.
        </p>
        <a href={`${root}/skills/run-durable-research/SKILL.md`}>Read the skill contract</a>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <button
          class="tra__expand"
          type="button"
          data-expand-image
          aria-label="Expand the completed Workflow screenshot"
        >
          <img
            src={`${root}/deck-assets/workflow-completed.png`}
            alt="Recorded demo frame showing both episode branches and both series reviews completed"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <span>Open full view</span>
        </button>
        <figcaption>Both episode branches and both series reviews completed in the original Workflow Execution.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="tra__section">
      <header class="tra__section-head">
        <p class="kicker">Observed recovery</p>
        <h2>Event History records the handoff</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="tra__evidence">
        <figure>
          <button
            class="tra__expand"
            type="button"
            data-expand-image
            aria-label="Expand the Worker failure screenshot"
          >
            <img
              src={`${root}/deck-assets/worker-killed.png`}
              alt="Terminal showing the Worker killed while two Activities are in flight"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <span>Open full view</span>
          </button>
          <figcaption>The Workflow remains open after the Worker receives SIGKILL.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <button
            class="tra__expand"
            type="button"
            data-expand-image
            aria-label="Expand the Temporal Web retry screenshot"
          >
            <img
              src={`${root}/deck-assets/activity-attempt-two.png`}
              alt="Temporal Web showing two research Activities starting on attempt two"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <span>Open full view</span>
          </button>
          <figcaption>Event History shows both <code>research_episode</code> Activities on attempt 2.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <aside class="tra__boundary" aria-labelledby="runtime-boundary">
      <h2 id="runtime-boundary">Runtime boundary</h2>
      <p>
        This page publishes the source and captured evidence as documentation.
        The live research integration runs on the configured workstation.
        <a href="https://www.sjarmak.ai/projects/scix-agent">SciX</a> and
        <a href="https://www.sjarmak.ai/projects/code-intelligence-digest">Code Intelligence Digest</a>
        depend on local repositories, indexes, databases, services, and Worker
        configuration that are not included here.
      </p>
    </aside>

  </article>

  <dialog id="evidence-viewer" class="tra-viewer" aria-label="Expanded evidence screenshot">
    <button class="tra-viewer__close" type="button" data-close-viewer>
      Close <span aria-hidden="true">×</span>
    </button>
    <figure>
      <img alt="" />
      <figcaption></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </dialog>
</PageLayout>

<script>
  const viewer = document.querySelector<HTMLDialogElement>("#evidence-viewer");
  const viewerImage = viewer?.querySelector<HTMLImageElement>("img");
  const viewerCaption = viewer?.querySelector<HTMLElement>("figcaption");
  const closeButton = viewer?.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-close-viewer]");

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-expand-image]").forEach((trigger) => {
    trigger.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const image = trigger.querySelector<HTMLImageElement>("img");
      const caption = trigger.closest("figure")?.querySelector("figcaption");
      if (!viewer || !viewerImage || !viewerCaption || !image) return;

      viewerImage.src = image.currentSrc || image.src;
      viewerImage.alt = image.alt;
      viewerCaption.textContent = caption?.textContent ?? "";
      viewer.showModal();
    });
  });

  closeButton?.addEventListener("click", () => viewer?.close());
  viewer?.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
    if (event.target === viewer) viewer.close();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .tra {
    --stack-gap: clamp(var(--space-xl), 8vw, var(--space-3xl));
    padding-block-end: var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .tra__artifacts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    border-block: var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .tra__artifacts a {
    display: flex;
    min-height: 4.5rem;
    padding: var(--space-s);
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-s);
    border-inline-end: var(--border-hairline);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .tra__artifacts a:last-child {
    border-inline-end: 0;
  }

  .tra__artifacts a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-bg-subtle);
  }

  .tra__media,
  .tra__evidence figure,
  .tra__skill figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .tra__media video {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .tra__premise {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .tra__section {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-l);
  }

  .tra__section-head {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .tra__section-head .kicker {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-xs);
  }

  .tra__section-head h2 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .tra__section-head > p:last-child {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-s);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .tra__code {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-l);
  }

  .tra__code section {
    min-width: 0;
    padding-block-start: var(--space-s);
    border-top: var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .tra__code h3 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-s);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .tra__code pre {
    min-height: 15rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-s);
    padding: var(--space-m);
    overflow: auto;
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .tra__skill {
    grid-template-columns: 5fr 7fr;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .tra__skill-copy {
    max-width: 38rem;
  }

  .tra__skill-copy > * + * {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-m);
  }

  .tra__skill img,
  .tra__evidence img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .tra__expand {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: transparent;
    color: inherit;
    cursor: zoom-in;
  }

  .tra__expand span {
    position: absolute;
    inset: auto var(--space-xs) var(--space-xs) auto;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.55rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-bg) 88%, transparent);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    line-height: 1;
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(0.25rem);
    transition:
      opacity 160ms ease-out,
      transform 160ms ease-out;
  }

  .tra__expand:hover span,
  .tra__expand:focus-visible span {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }

  .tra__expand:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .tra__evidence {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-l);
  }

  .tra-viewer {
    position: fixed;
    width: min(96vw, 96rem);
    max-width: none;
    height: min(94dvh, 60rem);
    max-height: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--space-m);
    inset: 50% auto auto 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    background: var(--color-bg);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .tra-viewer::backdrop {
    background: oklch(0.12 0.01 70 / 0.84);
  }

  .tra-viewer figure {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    height: 100%;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .tra-viewer img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    min-height: 0;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  .tra-viewer__close {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 1;
    inset: var(--space-xs) var(--space-xs) auto auto;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.7rem;
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-bg);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .tra-viewer__close:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .tra__boundary {
    padding-block: var(--space-l);
    border-block: var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .tra__boundary h2 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-s);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }

  .tra__boundary p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .tra__artifacts,
    .tra__code,
    .tra__skill,
    .tra__evidence {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .tra__artifacts a {
      border-inline-end: 0;
      border-bottom: var(--border-hairline);
    }

    .tra__artifacts a:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .tra-viewer {
      width: 100vw;
      height: 100dvh;
      padding: var(--space-s);
      border: 0;
      border-radius: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
